Modified-file notices (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

Section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0 requires that any modified file
distributed as part of a Derivative Work carry a prominent notice stating that
it was changed. Each file in section 1 above will carry the following notice
when it ships, placed right after its YAML frontmatter as an HTML comment so it
stays in the source without changing how the file renders:

  <!--
  Derived from <upstream path> in anthropics/claude-plugins-official
  (https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/apache-2.0.txt).
  Modified for agentrc: <one line describing the change>.
  -->

For a file listed as "verbatim apart from added lines", the change line reads
"Modified for agentrc: lines added; upstream text unchanged." Files derived
from the MIT-licensed projects in sections 2 and 3 need no per-file notice.
Their license and copyright notice travel with agentrc in the licenses/
directory and in this file.
